# Production-shaped ledger churn — the scenario the byte-identity gate needs.
#
# Generated (see git history for the generator); edit by regenerating, not by hand.
#
# The hand-written scenarios each touch two or three accounts and never release enough holds to
# resize a map. Real accounts do: they are first touched in whatever order they trade, and they
# place and release hundreds of holds. Both of those make an engine's hash-table layout a function
# of its HISTORY, so a node restored from a snapshot lays out differently from one that replayed
# from genesis — identical ledger, different snapshot bytes. This scenario reproduces that shape so
# SnapshotReplayEquivalenceTest actually bites.

CLOCK 1000

# --- 16 accounts, first touched in a scrambled order (not ascending userId) ---
DEPOSIT u=11 asset=0 amt=1000000.0
DEPOSIT u=11 asset=1 amt=10.0
DEPOSIT u=48 asset=0 amt=1000000.0
DEPOSIT u=48 asset=1 amt=10.0
DEPOSIT u=85 asset=0 amt=1000000.0
DEPOSIT u=85 asset=1 amt=10.0
DEPOSIT u=21 asset=0 amt=1000000.0
DEPOSIT u=21 asset=1 amt=10.0
DEPOSIT u=58 asset=0 amt=1000000.0
DEPOSIT u=58 asset=1 amt=10.0
DEPOSIT u=95 asset=0 amt=1000000.0
DEPOSIT u=95 asset=1 amt=10.0
DEPOSIT u=31 asset=0 amt=1000000.0
DEPOSIT u=31 asset=1 amt=10.0
DEPOSIT u=68 asset=0 amt=1000000.0
DEPOSIT u=68 asset=1 amt=10.0
DEPOSIT u=4 asset=0 amt=1000000.0
DEPOSIT u=4 asset=1 amt=10.0
DEPOSIT u=41 asset=0 amt=1000000.0
DEPOSIT u=41 asset=1 amt=10.0
DEPOSIT u=78 asset=0 amt=1000000.0
DEPOSIT u=78 asset=1 amt=10.0
DEPOSIT u=14 asset=0 amt=1000000.0
DEPOSIT u=14 asset=1 amt=10.0
DEPOSIT u=51 asset=0 amt=1000000.0
DEPOSIT u=51 asset=1 amt=10.0
DEPOSIT u=88 asset=0 amt=1000000.0
DEPOSIT u=88 asset=1 amt=10.0
DEPOSIT u=24 asset=0 amt=1000000.0
DEPOSIT u=24 asset=1 amt=10.0
DEPOSIT u=61 asset=0 amt=1000000.0
DEPOSIT u=61 asset=1 amt=10.0

# --- churn: 40 holds per account, all but every 10th released ---
# The map grows to hold 40 and keeps that capacity after the releases; an engine restored from the
# snapshot rebuilds the same 4 holds into a small map. Same reservations, different table, and
# therefore a different iteration order unless serialization imposes one.
